#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Kiro single review pass of an externally drafted plan (ChatPRD). Usage: bash scripts/coord/kiro-plan-review.sh <name> <plan-file>
source "$(dirname "$0")/kiro-run-common.sh"
N="${1:?name}"; F="${2:?plan file}"
OUT=docs/coordination/reviews/plan-$N.md
P="You are the PLAN REVIEWER for Agent Mesh v1. Do not modify any file except writing your review to $OUT. Do not write code, commit or dispatch.
The plan under review is $F, drafted by an external planner (ChatPRD, Claude Opus 5.5) that could NOT read the repo; it worked only from a context pack. Your job: one thorough review pass against the real repo.
Read docs/requirements.md, docs/plan.md (§14 adapters, §16 milestones M3, and all sections the plan cites), docs/acceptance-checklist.md (N-items, A-items), docs/HANDOFF.md, docs/QUEST-HANDOFF.md, docs/m1c-gate-report.md (adopted-wrapper residual), docs/coordination/plans/m2-plan.md (format, r10-r12 scope still pending), docs/impl-notes-m2-*.md, and the code the plan names (mesh/adapters/*, mesh/daemon/supervisor.py parse_run_output, adapter_probes writes, mesh/core/repos.py submission git info, tests/fixtures/real/, scripts/test.sh, tests/run_tier.py).
Check: (1) every factual claim about current code/files/functions/flags (the planner flagged unverified ones); (2) scope fits M3-lite and the Kiroween deadline (Dec 4 14:00 PT), gate Nov 16-17 realistic; (3) each run is small enough for one coder session, has disjoint FILES for the stated parallel pairs, and does not collide with pending M2 r10-r12 files; (4) acceptance items N18-N27 are testable and map to runs; (5) coordinator steps C0-C6 and consent gates are safe (real vendor runs only by the coordinator, credit ceilings); (6) A1 600 s suite budget respected (mock/fixture tests only in the default suite); (7) never-edit rules respected (tests/fixtures/real/** only by coordinator); (8) answer Q9 (does supervisor.parse_run_output use RunResult.final_text when non-empty), Q10 (how adapter_probes rows are written and whether the N1 test probes under tripwire shims) and Q11 (does a code-task submission require executor git commits; check repos.py/submission paths) from the code with file:line.
Write $OUT: first line exactly 'VERDICT: ACCEPT' or 'VERDICT: REVISE'; then a findings list (severity BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR, plan section, evidence file:line, required change); answers to Q9-Q11 with evidence; a list of exact edits to apply to the plan; and a list of decisions that need James."
run_kiro "$OUT" "$P" "planreview-$N"
